cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sloth-loop: an LLM-free, self-evolving task-orchestration engine"
message: "If you use sloth-loop in academic or production work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "lv"
    given-names: "fushuai"
    alias: "gege-lv"
version: "4.0-dev"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gege-lv/sloth-loop"
url: "https://github.com/gege-lv/sloth-loop"
abstract: >-
  sloth-loop turns a repeated analytical workflow (distribute candidates ->
  run -> judge -> distil rules) into a reusable, self-evolving process.  It is
  deliberately LLM-free: the engine orchestrates, the mounted agent thinks.
keywords:
  - orchestration
  - ooda
  - self-evolving
  - agent
  - automation
